{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":22,"code":"SNG","name":"Song of Songs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":2,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"SNG 2:1"},"I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," the rose of Sharon, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," the lily of the valleys. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"SNG 2:2"},"As the lily among thorns, so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," my love among the daughters. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"SNG 2:3"},"As the apple tree among the trees of the wood, so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," my beloved among the sons. I sat down under his shadow with great delight, and his fruit ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["was"]}," sweet to my taste. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"SNG 2:4"},"He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["was "]},"love. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"SNG 2:5"},"Stay me with flagons, comfort me with apples: for I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," sick of love. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"SNG 2:6"},"His left hand ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," under my head, and his right hand doth embrace me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"SNG 2:7"},"I charge you, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awake ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," love, till he please. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"SNG 2:8"},"The voice of my beloved! behold, he cometh leaping upon the mountains, skipping upon the hills. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"SNG 2:9"},"My beloved is like a roe or a young hart: behold, he standeth behind our wall, he looketh forth at the windows, shewing himself through the lattice. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"SNG 2:10"},"My beloved spake, and said unto me, Rise up, my love, my fair one, and come away. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"SNG 2:11"},"For, lo, the winter is past, the rain is over ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," gone; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"SNG 2:12"},"The flowers appear on the earth; the time of the singing ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of birds "]},"is come, and the voice of the turtle is heard in our land; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"SNG 2:13"},"The fig tree putteth forth her green figs, and the vines ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["with "]},"the tender grape give a ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["good"]}," smell. Arise, my love, my fair one, and come away. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:13"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"SNG 2:14"},"O my dove, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that art"]}," in the clefts of the rock, in the secret ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["places"]}," of the stairs, let me see thy countenance, let me hear thy voice; for sweet ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," thy voice, and thy countenance ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is "]},"comely. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"SNG 2:15"},"Take us the foxes, the little foxes, that spoil the vines: for our vines ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["have"]}," tender grapes. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:15"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"SNG 2:16"},"My beloved ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," mine, and I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," his: he feedeth among the lilies. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"SNG 2:17"},"Until the day break, and the shadows flee away, turn, my beloved, and be thou like a roe or a young hart upon the mountains of Bether. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 2:17"}]}]}
